---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy - Flightbook',
  description: 'Flightbook privacy policy - How we collect, use, and protect your personal data',
  robots: {
    index: true,
    follow: true,
  },
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 mx-auto lg:px-8 lg:py-20 max-w-4xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold leading-tighter tracking-tighter mb-8 font-heading">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p class="text-muted mb-8">Effective date: April 22, 2026</p>

    <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p>
        Flightbook operates the Flightbook application (the "Service"). This privacy policy explains how we collect,
        use, and protect your personal data when you use our Service.
      </p>
      <p>
        By using Flightbook, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

      <h3>Personal Data</h3>
      <p>We may collect the following personal data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>User account information</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Usage Data</h3>
      <p>
        We may collect technical information such as IP address, browser type, device information, and usage patterns to
        improve the Service.
      </p>

      <h3>Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        We use cookies and similar technologies to operate and improve the Service. You can control the use of cookies
        through your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>How We Use Data</h2>
      <p>We use the collected data to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide and maintain the Service</li>
        <li>Manage scheduling and appointments</li>
        <li>Improve features and user experience</li>
        <li>Provide customer support</li>
        <li>Ensure security and prevent abuse</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Google Calendar Integration</h2>
      <p>
        Flightbook integrates with Google Calendar to let users sync flight lesson appointments. Access to Google user
        data is granted only with the user's explicit consent via OAuth.
      </p>
      <p>We request the following permissions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>calendar.events</strong> – to create and update calendar events</li>
        <li><strong>calendar.readonly</strong> – to retrieve the list of available calendars</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Flightbook uses Google Calendar data solely for the purpose of syncing lesson appointments. Flightbook does not
        read, import, or analyze existing calendar events.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google user data is not used for advertising, profiling, or analytics unrelated to the Service's core
        functionality. No Google user data is sold or shared with third parties.
      </p>

      <h2>Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain personal data only as long as necessary to provide the Service. Minimal data such as calendar event
        identifiers may be stored to maintain synchronization.
      </p>
      <p>You can disconnect your Google account at any time, which stops any further access to Google data.</p>

      <h2>Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>We do not sell or rent your personal data.</p>
      <p>
        We may share data with trusted service providers only to the extent necessary to operate the Service. These
        providers are required to protect your data.
      </p>

      <h2>Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
      <p>We process personal data based on user consent and for the performance of our services.</p>

      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access your personal data</li>
        <li>Request correction or deletion of your data</li>
        <li>Withdraw your consent at any time</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data Security</h2>
      <p>We implement appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect your personal data.</p>

      <h2>International Data Transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Your data may be processed in Switzerland or in other countries where data protection laws may differ. We ensure
        that appropriate safeguards are in place.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>The Service may contain links to external websites. We are not responsible for their privacy practices.</p>

      <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. Updates will be posted on this page with a revised effective date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>If you have any questions about this privacy policy, please contact us:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:yannick.lagger@flightbook.ch">yannick.lagger@flightbook.ch</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
